<<~ ahu slot=`#/a-a-browser-mode-tw5-fed-by-the-port-alone`>>

!! A. A browser-mode TW5 fed by the port alone

!!! A0. The cause of the lends: the floor holds, with one refinement

The floor named `configureIslandRuntime` as the cause. Confirmed, and the page path carries a second forge-shaped cause upstream of it.

* The page branch boots with the ''Worker's'' boot env: `prepareHostBootInstance` calls `loadTiddlyWikiFromBlob(coreBlob, makeBrowserWorkerBootEnv())` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-host-bridge.ts:476`).
* That env pre-seeds `$tw` with `node: {}, browser: null` (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:299`) and hands the blob a `process` shim object (`:303`).
* So `bootprefix.js` skips its own detection (`TiddlyWiki5/boot/bootprefix.js:30-35` read `"browser" in $tw` / `"node" in $tw`). With `$tw.node` truthy it then reads bare `global.window` (`bootprefix.js:36`). ''That line is the `global is not defined in the boot prefix` the lane measured.''
* After eval, `configureIslandRuntime` nulls both flags (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:396-397`). Every module then executes with `Buffer: $tw.browser ? undefined : Buffer` (`boot/boot.js:862`) and `process: process` (`boot.js:876-879`): ''the `Buffer` and `process` lends.''
* With a `process` global standing, `$tw.utils.nextTick` takes the `process.nextTick` branch (`core/modules/utils/utils.js:706-713`); the shim's `nextTick` queues a microtask (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:171`). That covers ''`setImmediate` / `clearImmediate`''.

Stock browser detection reads `typeof window` / `typeof document` and `typeof process === "object"` (`bootprefix.js:30-35`). So the cure takes three moves, not one:
# A ''page boot env'': no `node`/`browser` pre-seed (or `node: null` alone); no `process` parameter; the real `window`, not the scoped lend.
# ''No `configureIslandRuntime`'' on the page path.
# ''No lends.''

Nothing found contradicts the floor.

One hazard: if any page bundle defines a global `process` object (Vite/rolldown injected one into the Worker bundle, `tw5-host-bridge.ts:441-443`), stock detection sets `$tw.node = {}` and the boot takes the Node branch. A pre-seed of `node: null` alone states a measured fact (this realm holds no Node) and closes that hazard.

''What browser mode still writes onto the page window.'' These are stock TW5's own claims, not lends:
* `window.$tw` and `window.sjcl` (the core blob carries sjcl).
* `window.onerror` (`boot.js:252-256`, from `trapErrors`, which `bootprefix.js:39-42` sets true in browser mode).
* `window.onbeforeunload` (`bootprefix`/`boot.js:2524-2535`).
* One hidden `PasswordPrompt` div on `document.body` (`boot.js:644-652, 2762-2765`).
* `document.title` and a `<style>` in `document.head`, but only if the `render` module runs.

The house's own unload hold (`packages/lararium-web/src/page-mirror.ts:31-33`) sits beside TW5's `onbeforeunload`. That is safe only while no TW5 unload task returns a message (see `saver-handler` below).

!!! A1. Walk of the boot and startup modules

Startup modules carry `platforms`; `$tw.boot.doesTaskMatchPlatform` gates them (`boot.js:2658-2680`), and `$tw.boot.disabledStartupModules` (a name list, honoured at `boot.js:2579, 2692, 2699`) removes any by name. Both mechanisms belong to TW5 and leave the engine's bytes, and so its CID, unchanged.

| Piece | What it does in browser mode | Mirror wants it? | How it stays out cleanly |h
| `bootprefix` platform detect (`bootprefix.js:30-42`) | sets `browser`, `node`, `trapErrors`, `readBrowserTiddlers` | yes | pre-seed `node: null` only |
| autoboot (`boot.js:2777`) | `$tw.boot.boot()` on eval | no; the house boots by hand | pre-seed `boot.suppressBoot` (already done, `tw5-host-bridge.ts:299`) |
| `trapErrors` → `window.onerror` (`boot.js:252`) | claims the page's error handler; error forms go on `document.body` (`boot.js:203-242`) | ''open (Q-A3)'' | flips only between bootprefix and `_boot`, so it needs a pre-seed hook; else accept it as stock |
| `decryptEncryptedTiddlers`, browser (`boot.js:1742`) | reads `#encryptedStoreArea`; absent → callback | harmless | the page carries no such element |
| `loadTiddlersBrowser` (`boot.js:1846-1862`), the DOM store-area reader | ingests `#storeArea`, `#styleArea`, `script.tiddlywiki-tiddler-store`, … from the ''page'' document | no; the port and `preloadTiddlers` feed it (`boot.js:2547`) | the page carries none of those selectors (a witness should assert it); the current no-op override (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:402`) belongs to the forge |
| `PasswordPrompt` (`boot.js:2762`) | one hidden div in `document.body` | no | unavoidable in stock browser mode; harmless |
| `load-modules` (`core/modules/startup/load-modules.js`) | applies `utils-browser`, builds `$tw.rootWidget` with the real `document` | ''yes'' | stock |
| `startup` (`startup/startup.js:17-131`) | UA detect, language/theme switchers, keyboard manager on `document`, StartupActions (`/Browser` too), ''syncadaptor search, Syncer, SaverHandler'', Popup, Animator | yes, except the sync/save tail | see the syncer and saver rows below; disabling `startup` would cost the whole module |
| `rootwidget` (`startup/rootwidget.js`) | `tm-http-request`, `tm-modal`, `tm-notify`, `tm-copy-to-clipboard`, `tm-focus-selector`, rename/relink, `tm-scroll`, `tm-full-screen` | ''yes'': this is most of G3's owed doors, for free | stock; but the camera must parent to `$tw.rootWidget` rather than mint its own root (`glass-camera.ts:34-35`) |
| `story` (`startup/story.js`) | permalink/permaview ''writes `location.hash`'', `hashchange` listener, `tm-browser-refresh` (reload), `tm-home`, `tm-print`, `tm-open-external-window` | partly. It wants story and history, but ''the page URL belongs to DreamDOM's route door'' | ''open (Q-A2)''; `$:/config/Navigation/UpdateAddressBar` = `no` keeps the hash write out by config (`startup/story.js:25`) |
| `render` (`startup/render.js`) | `document.title`, a `<style>` in `document.head`, the page template into `document.body`, the draft-throttled refresh, `th-page-refreshed` and `PostRender` actions | its ''behaviour'' yes; its ''DOM target'' no (the mirror paints into a shadow root) | `disabledStartupModules: ["render"]`, with the camera taking its place, ''but the camera must then emit the same hooks and actions'' (`th-page-refreshing`/`th-page-refreshed`, `$:/tags/StartupAction/PostRender`, the draft throttle). Plugins lean on them. The current camera emits none (`glass-camera.ts`) |
| `favicon` (`startup/favicon.js`) | writes `#faviconLink` if it exists | optional | no-op unless the page carries that id |
| `password` (`startup/password.js`) | `tm-set-password` / `tm-clear-password` → `$tw.crypto` (encrypts saved HTML) | ''no'': the house seals | `disabledStartupModules: ["password"]` |
| `browser-messaging` (`startup/browser-messaging.js`) | iframe loader for plugin libraries (`tm-load-plugin-library`) | ''open'': it serves the "people customize" road; installs land as wiki changes and so as port writes | stock, or disable by name; ties to Q-B |
| `windows` (`startup/windows.js`) | `tm-open-window` (`window.open`), unload task | yes (stock behaviour) | stock |
| `eventbus`, `confirm`, `info`, `plugins` | fork-era buses, the `tm-confirm` door, `$:/info`, plugin switching | yes | stock |
| ''syncer'' (`core/modules/syncer.js`) | built only if some module of type `syncadaptor` exports `adaptorClass` (`startup.js:104-118`) | ''no (ruled)'' | ship none. A shadow module drops when an ordinary tiddler of the same title overrides it (`boot.js:1539-1552`). The real risk: a ''person's plugin'' that carries a `syncadaptor` (the tiddlyweb plugin, for one) switches the syncer on silently. ''Open (Q-A1).'' |
| ''saver-handler'' (`core/modules/saver-handler.js:17-111`) | built ''unconditionally'' (`startup.js:120-124`). In browser mode it runs `initSavers` (every `saver` module), and with no syncadaptor it runs dirty tracking: a change listener, `tc-dirty` on `document.body`, an ''unload task that raises "unsaved changes"'', and the `tm-save-wiki` / `tm-download-file` / `tm-auto-save-wiki` handlers | ''no'' (ruled) for saving; `tm-download-file` stays wanted as the download door | Config, no core patch: shadow-override `$:/config/SaverFilter` to an empty filter. The handler then counts nothing, never dirties, and its unload task returns nothing (`saver-handler.js:30-90`). Set `$:/config/AutoSave` = `no`. Drop `saver` modules by same-title ordinary-tiddler overrides (`boot.js:1543`). The handler object still stands, inert. |

!!! A2. Writes out, landings in, no echo

The house already holds the end-state. It does not use the syncer.

* ''Out:'' `makeGlassPortAdaptor` listens on `wiki.addEventListener("change")` and posts one `port:write` per title, one write in flight per title; later keystrokes wait behind it, and the follow-up carries the latest image (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/glass-port-adaptor.ts:108-143`).
* ''In:'' `land()` calls `wiki.addTiddler` / `deleteTiddler` and ''tags two images'': the wire fields, and the tiddler as TW5 reads it back after normalising tags, lists and dates. `onChange` consumes a matching tag instead of posting (`glass-port-adaptor.ts:78-124`). Its own echo comes back as `causedBy` txIds and marks the pending write `echoed` (`:176-181`).
* ''Local-only titles'' (`$:/StoryList`, `$:/HistoryList`, `$:/temp`-style prefixes) never cross (`:73-75`).

That shape rhymes with what TW5's syncer itself does. `storeTiddler` records `tiddlerInfo[title] = {revision, changeCount: wiki.getChangeCount(title)}`, and a title reads dirty only when `getChangeCount(title) > tiddlerInfo.changeCount` (https://github.com/TiddlyWiki/TiddlyWiki5/blob/master/core/modules/syncer.js, &#126;L215, L254-264, L490; the line numbers come from upstream master). The `"change"` event fires batched on `nextTick` after `changeCount` bumps (`core/modules/wiki.js` `enqueueTiddlerEvent`), so an "applying remote" flag set around `addTiddler` has already cleared when the event fires. Both the image tags and a changeCount snapshot survive that delay. A cheap second witness: record `getChangeCount(title)` after each `land()` and drop any change event at or below it.

The image-tag approach is stronger than a changeCount for a CRDT, because a landing that TW5 rewrites (tag or list normalisation) still matches. Browser mode changes none of this. One seam moves: `nextTick` goes back to `window.setTimeout(fn,0)` once no `process` stands (`utils.js:709-711`). The mirror already overrides it to `queueMicrotask` (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:479`), a `$tw` property assignment and no byte change. Keep it, so event batching matches the island.

!!! A3. Prior art

See ''§A3-prior-art'' at the end; the TW5 prior-art agent's report folds in there.

