<<~ ahu slot=`#/c-golden-principles-and-pattern-integrities`>>

!! C. Golden principles and pattern integrities

# ''POLA: authority by reference, not by ambient reach.'' Sources: Miller, //Robust Composition//, http://www.erights.org/talks/thesis/ (UNVERIFIED, page not opened); Endo/SES docs above.
#* ''Rhymes with'' "no keys, no truth, the port alone": the port works as a capability.
#* ''Strains'' under "privilege stays open": the realm's //ambient// authority (origin storage) overrides the port's discipline. The port names what the mirror //should// use; the origin hands it everything.
# ''Confinement belongs to the platform, not to discipline.'' Figma's lesson: a JS-level realm shim on the main thread lost to one escape (Figma blog above). Logseq's iframe sandbox escaped by attribute injection when CSP stood off, CVE-2026-47901 (https://www.incibe.es/en/incibe-cert/early-warning/vulnerabilities/cve-2026-47901).
#* ''Rhymes with'' the lane's own line: "today the code keeps that by discipline, and the page realm enforces none of it" (`d3-glass-lane.mem` #/the-mirror-realm).
# ''Put the boundary where the secret lives, not where the guest lives'' (the key-side inversion, the wallet industry's convergence). When the guest must keep full DOM power (people customize TW5), move the //keys// out, not the guest in.
#* ''Rhymes with'' the Mu ruling on iframes for the //mirror//, and with "share substrate, not sovereignty".
#* ''Strains'' under isomorphic-by-intent (custody read by capability, never by host), unless the key origin presents the //same// custody capability on every vessel setup.
# ''Membranes wrap whole object graphs'' (Miller/Tribble; Agoric). The port already acts as a membrane of structured-clone data: no object identity crosses. ''Rhymes with'' "fed by the port alone". It argues against any shortcut that hands the mirror a live object from the island or custody.
# ''Local-first: the user owns the data, which lives on their devices; the network stays optional'' (Ink & Switch, https://www.inkandswitch.com/local-first/, UNVERIFIED, page not opened).
#* ''Rhymes with'' the house's own CRDT store over TW5's syncer and savers. TW5's savers presume a //file// as the truth; the house's truth sits in the CRDT, so saver paths stay out by principle, not taste.
# ''Process/host separation for extensions'' (VS Code's extension host; MV3 bans remote code and `eval` in extension pages, https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/migrate/improve-security).
#* ''Strains'' against TW5, whose plugin model //is// `eval` of wiki-carried code. Any MV3-style rule breaks the customization road.
#* ''Rhymes with'' "the engine stays byte-identical by CID": what loads gets //named by hash//, the TW5 analogue of "no remote code".
# ''One shape across setups.'' A design that holds only on the node's own box (setup 1) and fails the anon-device vessel (setup 2) breaks the boot/width/caps single pattern integrity (WIDTH RULING 3).
#* Full-trust acceptance holds in setup 1 and fails in setups 2 and 4.
#* The key-side inversion holds in setups 2 to 4 and stands moot in setup 1. It never contradicts any of them.
# ''No global now.'' TW5's `render` throttles draft refresh with `setTimeout(…,400)` (`startup/render.js`), `nextTick` uses `setTimeout(fn,0)`, and `tm-notify` dismisses on a timer.
#* A ''render cadence'' decides no truth, so it sits outside the no-global-now ruling's reach (a wall clock never //decides//).
#* Name it in the camera so a reader sees the line: timers pace paint, never truth.

---

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/leans`>>

!! Leans (each with what overturns it)

# ''Browser-mode boot:''
#* A page boot env of its own: pre-seed `{boot:{suppressBoot:true}, node:null}`, real `window`, no `process` parameter, no `configureIslandRuntime`, no lends.
#* `disabledStartupModules: ["render","password"]`.
#* `$:/config/SaverFilter` empty and `$:/config/AutoSave` `no` as shipped shadow overrides (house plugin tiddlers, not core bytes).
#* The camera mounts under `$tw.rootWidget` and emits `th-page-refreshing`/`th-page-refreshed` and `PostRender`.
#* //Overturn:// a measured plugin from the house's corpus that needs `render` itself (one that reads `$tw.pageContainer` or `$tw.styleElement`). Then the camera must set those names too, or `render` runs stock into a document the mirror owns.
# ''Syncer stays out by refusal, not by trust:'' at mount, a plugin census names any `syncadaptor` or `saver` module a person's plugin carries, and the mirror refuses to stand with it (a named floor: `none:plugin-syncadaptor`), or overrides it by same-title tiddler. //Overturn:// an operator ruling that a person's own syncadaptor counts as their intent.
# ''Stock writes on the page window'' (`$tw`, `sjcl`, `onerror`, `onbeforeunload`): accept them as TW5's own browser-mode claims, documented beside the house's unload hold. //Overturn:// a page library that also claims `onerror`/`onbeforeunload` by property, not by `addEventListener`.
# ''Privilege: the key-side inversion as the end-state, popup/top-level-first.''
#* A key origin, opened ''top-level'' for unlock and signing (dodging partitioning and Safari's ephemeral third-party storage), holds the custody rows.
#* The app origin, where the mirror and every plugin run, keeps only ciphertext CRDT chunks and public bytes.
#* The first step, with no second origin needed: ''seal the Automerge repo at rest'', and ''refuse the cleartext keystore'' on any vessel that runs the mirror at full width.
#* //Overturn:// a measured UX cost the operator refuses (a popup per session); or Safari Home Screen apps (exempt from the 7-day cap but separate from Safari) proving the only phone seat, which would push custody back into one origin and leave "accept full trust plus seal at rest" as the floor.
# ''Refuse SES and origin-per-wiki for the mirror.'' TW5's model (bare globals, `eval`, prototype extension) defeats SES without a DOM membrane no one has built. Origin-per-wiki multiplies the partition trap and breaks one-page transclusion. //Overturn:// a working SES DOM membrane in production, which this seat found none of.
# ''Trusted Types as a plugin-install choke point'', not as custody: one named policy through which every `new Function` of a module passes, hashed against the CID manifest. //Overturn:// measured breakage of stock widgets (TW5 sets `innerHTML` in places; UNVERIFIED in this fork's count).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/questions-only-the-operator-can-rule`>>

!! Questions only the operator can rule

* ''Q-A1.'' A person's plugin carrying a `syncadaptor` or `saver`: refuse the mirror, override by tiddler, or honour it as their intent?
* ''Q-A2.'' Does the mirror's story own the page URL hash (permalinks, `#:safe` safe mode, which itself acts as a URL-string boot switch rhyming with the refused `?glass=`), or does DreamDOM's route door own it, with `UpdateAddressBar` off?
* ''Q-A3.'' Do TW5's `window.onerror` claim and its error form on `document.body` stand (stock), or does the house own the page error rail? A pre-seeded `trapErrors:false` cannot ride `bootprefix.js:39`, which overwrites `tasks`; it would need a pre-`_boot` hook.
* ''Q-A4.'' Modals and notifications: stock `Modal`/`Notifier` append to `document.body` (`utils/dom/notifier.js:58`, `modal.js:30-50`), outside the shadow root and its stylesheet. Either the mirror owns the document (the stylesheet goes into `document.head`), or the shadow root holds the page and these doors re-route.
* ''Q-B1.'' Key-side inversion (a second origin, popup-first) versus full trust plus sealing at rest.
* ''Q-B2.'' Persona-root seeds rest cleartext //by ruling//. Does the mirror's arrival at full width (any person's plugin in the realm) re-open that ruling for browser vessels?
* ''Q-B3.'' Who serves the key origin on an anon-device vessel and a user-class cap-stack with no node infrastructure: the same static host under a sibling name, or a fixed house origin? This touches the DNS-01 and civic-TLS memos.

---

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/a3-prior-art`>>

!! §A3-prior-art

''Headline:'' this seat found ''no published TW5 build that runs without a syncer and is fed by an external CRDT.'' Every working integration goes through a `syncadaptor` plus `$tw.syncer`, or through a saver. The house's adaptor stands as its own prior art.

| Project | Store and sync | Takeaway for a port-fed mirror |h
| ''TiddlyPWA'' (https://codeberg.org/valpackett/tiddlypwa, `plugins/tiddlypwa/main.js`) | a `syncadaptor` whose "server" holds encrypted IndexedDB. Other tabs' changes arrive on BroadcastChannel into queues, drained through `$tw.syncer.syncFromServer()`. It ''shadows `$:/core/modules/savers/put.js` with a dummy'', because `put.js` probes the server from its constructor | ''The closest prior art.'' It proves the "port as the syncer's server" alternative, and it uses the same-title shadow override to kill a saver. The ruling keeps the syncer out, so it serves as a contrast, plus confirmation of the override technique. |
| ''TidGi'' (Electron; https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/tidgi@0.13.0-prerelease4/docs/internal/IPCSyncAdaptorAndFSAdaptor.md) | IPC syncadaptor; echo suppression by a `recentlySavedTiddlers` set plus a watcher exclusion list | "''timestamps proved unreliable''" for echo: matching by image or count beats `modified` |
| ''TiddlyDesktop'' (https://github.com/TiddlyWiki/TiddlyDesktop) | single-file wikis in iframes, saving through the TiddlyFox DOM-event protocol (`source/js/utils/saving.js`); folder wikis through the Node server and the tiddlyweb adaptor. Overhaul PR #327 adds Yjs co-editing over a `$tw.wiki` change listener that never broadcasts drafts (summary only, https://talk.tiddlywiki.org/t/tiddlydesktop-rs-tiddlydesktop-overhaul/15389, code UNVERIFIED) | the host catches whole-file saves, the opposite shape. PR #327's "change listener, drafts never cross" rhymes with the adaptor's `local()` titles; ''check whether the adaptor sends `draft.of` tiddlers'' |
| ''MultiWikiServer'' (https://github.com/TiddlyWiki/MultiWikiServer, `plugins/client/src/new-multiwikiclientadaptor.ts`) | syncadaptor under the stock syncer, plus SSE | Arlen22's design note names the syncer's ''one-tiddler-at-a-time'' saving as a bottleneck (https://mws.tiddlywiki.com/static/2025-05-06%2520-%2520syncer%2520design.html); TW5 PR #9117 (UNVERIFIED). Supports keeping the syncer out. |
| ''TW5-Bob'' (https://github.com/OokTech/TW5-Bob, `FileSystem/BrowserWSAdaptor.js`) | WebSocket syncadaptor; an ack per save; hash compare on reconnect | per-write acks rhyme with the port's txId answers |
| ''TW5-Yjs'' (the operator's own 2021 brainstorm, https://talk.tiddlywiki.org/t/tw5-yjs-real-time-sync-brainstorm/298) | fields as Yjs strings, forked from Bob; code status UNVERIFIED | linonetwo notes Yjs/yrs handles JSON well but plain wikitext poorly (https://talk.tiddlywiki.org/t/sharing-synchronizing-tiddlywikis-with-a-crdt-protocol/12324) |
| ''tiddlywiki-ipfs'' (https://github.com/xmaysonnave/tiddlywiki-ipfs) | a saver: each save makes a new CID, optionally published under IPNS | whole-file and content-addressed; not per-tiddler |
| ''Feather Wiki'' (https://codeberg.org/Alamantus/FeatherWiki) | one self-replicating HTML file; download, or a whole-file PUT | not a model |
| TW5 + Automerge, WebRTC plugins | none found | — |

''A gap the prior art flags:'' TiddlyPWA's `put.js` lesson applies here directly. In browser mode, `initSavers` ''constructs every saver'', and `put.js` fires network probes (OPTIONS/HEAD to the page URL) from its constructor (confirmed in this fork: `core/modules/savers/put.js:22-24` HEAD, `:49-51` OPTIONS; TiddlyPWA kills it the same way). An empty `SaverFilter` does ''not'' stop that. The mirror needs the saver modules overridden by same-title tiddlers (`boot.js:1543`), not just a filter.

<<~/ahu>>

